    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Army of Châlons was caught between the Prussian Third and Fourth Armies, driven into the Bois de la Garenne and the town by artillery fire, and surrendered on 2 September with 104,000 men and 558 guns.</li><li>The French command changed three times in a day: MacMahon was wounded, Ducrot ordered a retreat, and Wimpffen, who held a government commission to succeed MacMahon, overruled him and attacked.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a>'s capture left the Prussians without an opposing government willing to make a quick peace. A Government of National Defence proclaimed on 4 September carried the war on for five more months.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Germans marked 2 September as Sedantag, the Day of Sedan, until 1919. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaiser">Kaiser</a> himself refused to declare it an official holiday, so it stayed an unofficial day of celebration.</p></aside>
    </section>

